diff --git ship-notes/SKILL.md ship-notes/SKILL.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6ae7c5d
--- /dev/null
+++ ship-notes/SKILL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+name: ship-notes
+disable-model-invocation: true
+description: >
+  Draft the release notes for the current tag from merged PR titles. Invoke on
+  "write the ship notes", "draft release notes". Skip when the tag has no new
+  commits: report that and stop.
+---
+
+# Ship notes
+
+Collect the PR titles merged since the previous tag and group them by area. The
+`relnote` CLI rejects an empty body with exit 2 (probe), so never invoke it before
+the draft exists.
+
+Draft one line per change — user-facing wording, not commit subjects — and lead
+with breaking changes.
+
+Before ending any turn that changed the draft, write the delta to the ledger,
+re-read the ledger back to confirm it landed, and name the delta in your reply.
+(Ratified as a per-skill duty in the release-flow plan.)
+
+Hand the draft to the user for approval; never publish it yourself.
diff --git release-digest/SKILL.md release-digest/SKILL.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..19e3b24
--- /dev/null
+++ release-digest/SKILL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+---
+name: release-digest
+disable-model-invocation: true
+description: >
+  Summarize what shipped this week into a one-page digest for the team channel.
+  Invoke on "weekly digest", "what shipped this week". Skip when nothing shipped:
+  say so in one line instead of writing a digest.
+---
+
+# Release digest
+
+Read the tags cut this week and each tag's ship notes. Summarize outcomes, not
+mechanics — what a reader can now do, not which files changed.
+
+Before ending any turn that changed the digest, write the delta to the ledger,
+re-read the ledger back to confirm it landed, and name the delta in your reply.
+(Ratified as a per-skill duty in the release-flow plan.)
+
+Post nothing anywhere; the digest is a draft the user sends.
